{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1478757-acamoth-homebrew-abyssal-tutelage","id":1478757,"title":"Acamoth Homebrew: Abyssal Tutelage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-13T06:21:42-07:00","id":1478757,"title":"Acamoth Homebrew: Abyssal Tutelage","content":"I've always loved Abyssal Entities, but found Acamoth difficult to work into a chronicle. This homebrew outlines a system by which Acamoth can take up residence in a mage's Oneiros as a dark tutor, offering increasingly powerful Abyssal secrets and bonuses to antinomian magic according to Rank, while dragging their host closer to Rapture and the Abyss. Acamoth are bolstered by the defilement of Wisdom and may, once they gain enough power, Manifest themselves fully and toss aside a mage they seduced to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>ACAMOTH</b></span><br /> <br /> Acamoth strike deals with mages, offering knowledge and power in exchange for access to the Astral dreams of Awakened souls, through which they conjure the Abyss to infect the Astral Realms and empower themselves.<br /> <br /> Acamoth corrupt the host's Onerios to resemble the Abyss - conjuring horrifying nightmares in the process which make restful sleep impossible.<br /> <br /> These nightmares are horrifying and intense, usually themed according to the host's Vice through the lens of an Influence.<br /> <br /> Acamoth can teach a mage forbidden Abyssal lore and enhance a mage's ability to wield Paradox, though in doing so they strengthen their grip on the mage's soul and drag them closer to becoming Rapt and, potentially, a Qliphoth.<br /> <br /> As the host's connection to the Abyss deepens, the Acamoth becomes more powerful. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>SYSTEM</b></span><br /> <br /> Hosting an Acamoth in your Oneiros provides the following effects:<br /> <br /> \u2022 No Willpower gained from sleep<br /> \u2022 -[Rank] to Wisdom rolls<br /> \u2022 +[Rank] to Joining rolls<br /> \u2022 +[Rank] to control Paradox Reach.<br /> <br /> An Acamoth's Rank determines the Abyssal lore it can teach:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Rank 1-2: Teach Antinomian Sorcery<br /> \u2022 Rank 2-3: Teach Joining<br /> \u2022 Rank 3-4: Teach Abyssal Legacy<br /> \u2022 Rank 5: Teach path to Elder Diadem<br /> <br /> A host becoming Rapt, successfully Joining, or becoming a Qliphoth provides the Acamoth the following effects:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Increase Rank by 1, to a maximum of 5.<br /> \u2022 Gain a Manifestation.<br /> <br /> A Joined host can take the Acamoth as a Familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26991,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26991-dentedhelm","user":"Dentedhelm","date":". 04-14-2022, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26991-dentedhelm","name":"Dentedhelm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26991_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:51:02-07:00","id":1484029,"title":"","content":"I'm really digging this. It already has me thinking about how a clever Acamoth could trick one of my PCs into letting it take up roost in their Oneiros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:10:47-07:00","id":1484074,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that a side effect of not recovering Willpower means the mage will have to rely on Virtue, Vice and exceptional successes on spells to regain their motivation. This could visibly manifest as erratic behavior (indulging too often their Vice or pursuing their Virtue with sudden fervor) or being excessively devoted to casting the most precise Imago possible (chasing the +5 dice pool bonus). I am curious about one detail: Entities above Rank 2 cannot be made into familiars, does this supersede that ?<br /> <br /> I imagine any mage with caution or veterans in Abyssal magic would want some safeguard against the Acamoth betraying them, like some binding covenants, secret lore or forgotten secrets. So the ones that are not desperate for immediate results would likely seek those out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-14-2022, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T18:47:20-08:00","id":1497337,"title":"","content":"I am treating the Familiar rules similar to the Merit. They can have a Rank 1 Acamoth at Joining 2 and a Rank 2 at Joining 4. No Familiars beyond that rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}